<p class="chapo">@L.T("le-site-ne-juge-personne-il", "Le site ne juge personne : il affiche ce que la source publie. Quand une donnée est calculée, douteuse ou manquante, il le dit.", "The site judges no one: it displays what the source publishes. When a piece of data is calculated, doubtful or missing, it says so.")</p>

<section class="bloc-texte">
    <h2>@L.T("d-ou-viennent-les-donnees", "D'où viennent les données", "Where the data comes from")</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>@L.TH("chambre-des-deputes-source-officielle-l", "<strong>Chambre des députés</strong> : source <strong>officielle</strong>, l'open data de la Chambre (<a href=\"https://dati.camera.it/\">dati.camera.it</a>, point d'accès SPARQL), sous licence <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.fr\">CC BY-SA 4.0</a> : totaux officiels, résultat et vote de chaque député. Chaque vote renvoie à sa fiche officielle.", "<strong>Chamber of Deputies</strong>: <strong>official</strong> source, the Chamber's open data (<a href=\"https://dati.camera.it/\">dati.camera.it</a>, SPARQL endpoint), under the <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/\">CC BY-SA 4.0</a> licence: official totals, result and each deputy's vote. Each vote links to its official page.")</li>
        <li>@L.TH("senat-source-officielle-l-open-data", "<strong>Sénat</strong> : source <strong>officielle</strong>, l'open data du Sénat (<a href=\"https://dati.senato.it/\">dati.senato.it</a>, point d'accès SPARQL) : totaux, résultat, liste des sénateurs pour, contre et abstenus, <strong>mandats et groupes datés</strong>. Licence : <a href='https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/'>CC BY 3.0</a> (attribution), indiquée sur la page d'accueil de dati.senato.it.", "<strong>Senate</strong>: <strong>official</strong> source, the Senate's open data (<a href=\"https://dati.senato.it/\">dati.senato.it</a>, SPARQL endpoint): totals, result, the lists of senators for, against and abstaining, <strong>dated mandates and groups</strong>. Licence: <a href='https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/'>CC BY 3.0</a> (attribution), stated on the home page of dati.senato.it.")</li>
        <li>@L.T("mise-a-jour-automatique-chaque-nuit", "Mise à jour automatique chaque nuit : les votes de moins de sept jours sont relus. Le code est un logiciel libre (GPL-3.0).", "Automatic update every night: votes less than seven days old are read again. The code is free software (GPL-3.0).")</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="bloc-texte">
    <h2>@L.T("comment-se-lit-un-vote", "Comment se lit un vote", "How a vote is read")</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>@L.TH("senat-au-senat-les-abstentions-comptent", "<strong>Sénat</strong> : au Sénat, les <strong>abstentions comptent parmi les votants</strong> (votants = pour + contre + abstenus). Les mandats et les groupes viennent de la source, avec leurs dates : le groupe affiché est celui du sénateur <em>le jour du vote</em>. Un sénateur sans vote ni congé ce jour-là est absent, sans raison affichée. Un sénateur « en congé ou mission » apparaît absent.", "<strong>Senate</strong>: in the Senate, <strong>abstentions are counted among the voters</strong> (voters = for + against + abstentions). Mandates and groups come from the source, with their dates: the group shown is the senator's <em>on the day of the vote</em>. A senator with neither a vote nor leave that day is absent, with no reason shown. A senator “on leave or mission” appears absent.")</li>
        <li>@L.TH("favorable-contraire-abstention-tels-que-publ", "<strong>Favorable, contraire, abstention</strong> : tels que publiés. Les <strong>abstentions ne comptent pas</strong> parmi les votants : en Italie, votants = pour + contre, et les présents = votants + abstentions.", "<strong>In favour, against, abstention</strong>: as published. <strong>Abstentions are not counted</strong> among the voters: in Italy, voters = for + against, and those present = voters + abstentions.")</li>
        <li>@L.TH("absent-le-depute-siegeait-a-la", "<strong>Absent</strong> : le député siégeait à la date du vote mais n'a pas voté (« non ha votato », y compris « en mission »). Le site ne donne <em>aucune raison</em>.", "<strong>Absent</strong>: the deputy was in office on the date of the vote but did not vote (“non ha votato”, including “on mission”). The site gives <em>no reason</em>.")</li>
        <li>@L.TH("scrutin-secret-la-chambre-ne-publie", "<strong>Scrutin secret</strong> : la Chambre ne publie que les totaux, pas la position de chaque député. Le vote est affiché avec ses totaux, sans points, et marqué « décompte incomplet » : il n'entre dans aucun taux de participation.", "<strong>Secret ballot</strong>: the Chamber publishes only the totals, not each deputy's position. The vote is shown with its totals, without dots, and marked “incomplete count”: it enters no participation rate.")</li>
        <li>@L.TH("groupe-celui-du-depute-au-moment", "<strong>Groupe</strong> : celui du député au moment du vote, d'après la source ; « No group » = député sans groupe. <strong>Mandats</strong> : la source n'a pas d'annuaire daté ici ; un mandat va du premier au dernier vote <em>importé</em> où le député figure dans la liste (<strong>calculé par le site</strong>).", "<strong>Group</strong>: the deputy's group at the time of the vote, as given by the source; “No group” = deputy without a group. <strong>Mandates</strong>: the source has no dated directory here; a mandate runs from the first to the last <em>imported</em> vote where the deputy appears in the list (<strong>calculated by the site</strong>).")</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="bloc-texte">
    <h2>@L.T("calcule-par-le-site-non-publie", "Calculé par le site (non publié tel quel)", "Calculated by the site (not published as is)")</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>@L.T("le-resultat-adopte-rejete-et-le", "Le résultat « adopté / rejeté » et le seuil de majorité sont ceux de la Chambre ; le libellé « majorité simple des votants, abstentions exclues » est celui du site.", "The “adopted / rejected” result and the majority threshold are the Chamber's; the label “simple majority of those voting, abstentions not counted” is the site's.")</li>
        <li>@L.T("les-noms-sont-publies-en-majuscules", "Les noms sont publiés en majuscules par la source : la casse (« De Luca ») est refaite par le site.", "Names are published in capitals by the source: the capitalisation (“De Luca”) is rebuilt by the site.")</li>
        <li>@L.T("le-numero-d-un-vote-est", "Le numéro d'un vote est calculé par le site (séance × 10 000 + numéro du vote dans la séance) ; la note de chaque vote donne la séance et le numéro d'origine.", "The number of a vote is calculated by the site (sitting × 10,000 + vote number within the sitting); the note of each vote gives the original sitting and number.")</li>
        <li>@L.T("participation-parmi-les-deputes-en-fonction", "Participation : parmi les députés en fonction à la date d'un vote importé, la part de ceux qui ont voté. Les autres sont absents.", "Participation: among the deputies in office on the date of an imported vote, the share who voted. The others are absent.")</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="bloc-texte">
    <h2>@L.T("limites-connues", "Limites connues", "Known limits")</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>@L.TH("tous-les-votes-ne-sont-pas", "<strong>Tous les votes ne sont pas importés.</strong> Seuls les votes <em>finaux</em> (et, pour la Chambre, les <em>questions de confiance</em>) le sont pour l'instant ; les amendements, ordres du jour, motions et articles (la grande majorité des votes de la Chambre) ne le sont pas. Les taux de participation ne portent donc que sur ces votes.", "<strong>Not every vote is imported.</strong> Only <em>final votes</em> (and, for the Chamber, <em>confidence votes</em>) are for now; amendments, orders of the day, motions and articles (the large majority of the Chamber's votes) are not. Participation rates therefore only cover those votes.")</li>
        <li>@L.T("au-senat-seuls-les-votes-finaux", "Au Sénat, seuls les votes finaux (libellé « Votazione finale ») sont importés ; la source ne les marque pas autrement. Le titre d'un vote final est celui du projet de loi qui lui est relié, quand la source le donne.", "In the Senate, only final votes (label “Votazione finale”) are imported; the source marks them in no other way. The title of a final vote is that of the bill linked to it, when the source gives one.")</li>
        <li>@L.T("les-titres-sont-dans-la-langue", "Les titres sont dans la langue de la source (italien) ; certains caractères accentués peuvent être mal encodés dans la source.", "Titles are in the source's language (Italian); some accented characters may be badly encoded in the source.")</li>
        <li>@L.TH("pour-signaler-une-erreur-ecrivez-a", "Pour signaler une erreur, écrivez à <a href=\"mailto:contact@rebisway.com\">contact@rebisway.com</a>.", "To report an error, write to <a href=\"mailto:contact@rebisway.com\">contact@rebisway.com</a>.")</li>
    </ul>
</section>
}
else if (L.Pays == "GB" && L.Anglais)
{
<h1 class="titre-page">Methodology and limits</h1>
<p class="chapo">The site judges no one: it displays what the official source publishes. When a piece of data is calculated, doubtful or missing, it says so.</p>

<section class="bloc-texte">
    <h2>Where the data comes from</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>House of Commons divisions</strong>: the UK Parliament's public <a href="https://commonsvotes-api.parliament.uk/">Commons Votes API</a> (JSON), from the start of the 58th Parliament (17 December 2019) to today (the 59th opened on 9 July 2024). Contains Parliamentary information licensed under the <a href="https://www.parliament.uk/site-information/copyright-parliament/open-parliament-licence/">Open Parliament Licence v3.0</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>House of Lords divisions</strong>: the <a href="https://lordsvotes-api.parliament.uk/">Lords Votes API</a> (divisions: only the peers who voted are published, as Content or Not content) and the <a href="https://members-api.parliament.uk/">Members API</a> (dates of entry and exit of each peer). <strong>Absent peers are deduced</strong> from those membership dates and are not stored: peers on leave of absence or suspended cannot be told apart from absent ones, so absence rates in the Lords are overstated; each division says so. A peer's party is the latest one known (the votes carry the party of the day). The Lords have no recorded vote on the whole bill, so every division is shown and there is no &ldquo;whole bill&rdquo; filter.</li>
        <li><strong>Petitions</strong>: the public JSON of <a href="https://petition.parliament.uk/">petition.parliament.uk</a> (same licence): open and closed petitions with their supporters, the government response (from 10,000 supporters) and the debate (from 100,000). The site takes one snapshot a day and keeps all of them, so a drop in supporters can be shown; it is never explained, because the source gives no cause. Petitions rejected before publication are not imported; the history starts on the day of the first import.</li>
        <li>Automatic update: divisions less than seven days old are read again, because the source corrects its lists after publication. The <a href="https://github.com/rebisway/ilsontvote">code is free software</a> (GPL-3.0).</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="bloc-texte">
    <h2>How a division is read</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>For (aye), against (no)</strong>: as published in the division lists. Tellers, listed separately by the source, are counted on their side.</li>
        <li><strong>Both lobbies</strong>: a member listed in both the ayes and the noes voted in both lobbies, which parliamentary practice treats as an abstention. The site records an abstention and says so in the note of the division. There is no formal abstention in the Commons.</li>
        <li><strong>Absent</strong>: the member was in office on the date of the division but is in neither list. The source publishes a “no vote recorded” list (absent members, the Speaker and Deputy Speakers who do not vote, abstentionist members): the site gives <em>no reason</em> and shows all of them as absent.</li>
        <li><strong>Proxy</strong>: a member can vote through a colleague under the proxy voting scheme; the vote counts and is indicated.</li>
        <li><strong>Mandates</strong>: the source has no dated directory. A mandate runs from the first to the last division in which the member appears in any list (<strong>calculated by the site</strong>); the number of seats on a given day never exceeds 650.</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="bloc-texte">
    <h2>Calculated by the site (not published as is)</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Result “adopted / rejected”</strong>: computed from the official counts (more ayes than noes); a tie is left undetermined.</li>
        <li><strong>Participation</strong>: among the members in office on the date of a division, the share who voted (aye, no or both lobbies). The others are absent. Divisions whose lists are incomplete (see below) are not counted.</li>
        <li><strong>Seating chart</strong>: the government benches (left) and all other groups (right) are drawn as two facing crescents, one dot per member. Which group sits with the government is set by the site's administrator and revisited after each change of majority; within a side, groups are ordered by size. It is a layout, not the real bench position of each member.</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="bloc-texte">
    <h2>Known limits</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Incomplete lists</strong>: in most divisions the source names a few members fewer than its own official count (2.5 fewer on average). Such divisions are marked “incomplete count” and excluded from participation rates, because their absentees are not reliable.</li>
        <li><strong>Divisions only</strong>: votes without a recorded division (on the voices) leave no individual vote and do not appear.</li>
        <li><strong>History</strong>: the 58th and 59th Parliaments (since December 2019) are loaded; earlier ones are not. Bills are linked to divisions by title, a calculation made by this site (flagged as such on each division).</li>
        <li>To report an error, write to <a href="mailto:contact@rebisway.com">contact@rebisway.com</a>.</li>
    </ul>
</section>
}
